  "type": {
    "$comment": "Font families mirror AppFonts cascade. Web CJK fallbacks are the web-equivalent of the iOS per-locale cascade (PingFang TC / Noto Serif TC). Type scale mirrors AppFonts.TypeScale (the formal 7-step ramp) plus the vocab bespoke sizes (detail-word 27, row-word 18, section-title 18) from AppSkin.",
    "family": {
      "serif": "'Athelas', 'STSongti TC', 'Noto Serif TC', Georgia, serif",
      "sans": "'ElmsSans', 'PingFang TC', -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif",
      "italic": "'CormorantGaramond', Georgia, serif",
      "$comment-mono": "WORD-rendering monospace, mirrors iOS AppFonts.systemMono (.system design:.monospaced = SF Mono), NOT AppFonts.mono() (which is ElmsSans+sysMono cascade for IPA/code). The vocab word faces (rowWord/detailWord/reviewWord in AppSkin) all use systemMono, so the web stack leads with the system monospaced family. An earlier 'ElmsSans Mono' first entry was a ghost (no @font-face / no font file ever shipped) that always fell through to ui-monospace — removed so the stack honestly equals the SF-Mono SoT.",
      "mono": "ui-monospace, 'SF Mono', SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace",
      "$comment-display": "WEB-ONLY composite display/heading stack (no iOS SoT counterpart). Leads with the CormorantGaramond display face, then falls back through the serif body cascade. Used by the chrome-extension side panel + options headings so the brand serif lives in ONE place.",
      "display": "'CormorantGaramond', 'Athelas', 'Noto Serif TC', 'Songti TC', Georgia, serif"
    },
